      "section": "Military, defense & geopolitics",
      "headline": "Northrop Grumman says its YFQ-48A Talon Blue completed a first fully autonomous flight, taxi through landing",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "Northrop Grumman's release says its Talon Blue completed its first fully autonomous flight, including taxi, takeoff, in-flight manoeuvres, and landing. It flew from Mojave Air and Space Port, and it was built by Northrop's subsidiary Scaled Composites." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Who paid for it?" },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Northrop did. The War Zone reports Talon Blue was developed through company investment rather than under a government contract. It's aimed at the Air Force's Collaborative Combat Aircraft Increment 2, a competition whose requirements, The War Zone says, remain undefined." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Fully autonomous is a company claim about one test flight, and it is not independently verified. The release doesn't say what the aircraft decided for itself and what was pre-programmed, and gives no duration, altitude or speed. The 500,000 autonomous flight hours it cites is a company-wide total, not this aircraft's." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
      "section": "Military, defense & geopolitics",
      "headline": "North Korea claims artificial intelligence aboard an intermediate-range missile fired toward the East Sea",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "North Korea is now attaching an AI claim to a missile. Euronews reports an intermediate-range ballistic missile was launched early Saturday from the Wonsan area." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "South Korea's Joint Chiefs of Staff put the distance travelled at more than 700 kilometres. Japan's Defense Ministry estimated roughly 680 kilometres, and said it landed outside Japan's exclusive economic zone." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Kim Yo Jong said the missile can alter its trajectory at low altitudes, asserted unspecified artificial intelligence capabilities, and said there is no way to avoid this attack." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "That is Pyongyang's own claim, and it is not independently verified. Euronews is the one outlet whose timing we could confirm, so treat it as a single source, and it reports no technical analysis confirming or refuting the manoeuvring. South Korea's military often accuses the North of exaggerating its capabilities." }
      ]
    },
    {
