        { "host": "A", "text": "On water, he says direct data centre consumption is 0.5% of all industrial water usage in the United States. TechCrunch notes a planned Amazon data centre in Texas is permitted to release 33 million tons of carbon dioxide per year, more than any other power plant in the country. Garman's answer is that the generators are idle 99.9% of the time." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Those are Amazon's own numbers, none of them independently audited, and the water comparison is a share of industrial use, not of all water use. Only one outlet carried the post. TechCrunch's counterpoint: an independent watchdog said data centres were the main culprit behind a 76% year-over-year price increase on America's largest electrical grid. It's an update to yesterday's item on AWS dropping government NDAs." }
      ]
