      "headline": "Google cuts free Gemini users to Flash-Lite only from October 9, and takes Pro away from $4.99 subscribers",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "B", "text": "Google's Gemini support page says that starting in October 2026 there will be changes to model availability for the Gemini apps on a personal account, and that these changes start to take effect for users without a subscription on October 9th. With no plan, you're left with the Flash-Lite version of Gemini, losing Flash and Pro." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "AI Plus subscribers, at $4.99 a month, keep Flash-Lite and Flash but lose Pro. AI Pro, at $19.99 a month, and AI Ultra keep all three, and 9to5Google reports AI Pro also gains Deep Think, which had been restricted to the higher tier." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Google gives no reason for the change and publishes no usage-limit numbers for any tier. 9to5Google also reports the app is adding low, medium and high effort levels for each model, which will use more of your limit." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "item",
