      "headline": "ThinkingBox runs each of 507 business tasks 20 times: Claude Opus 5.5 leads at 67.16% but passes all 20 on only 241",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "A", "text": "Microsoft and Hugging Face released a benchmark called ThinkingBox, and the design is the point. It's 507 stateful business workflows across retail, auto insurance, travel, a neobank and consulting." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Each task runs 20 independent times, each one from an identical clean backend, and the grade comes from the state of the database afterwards and the side effects, not from what the model said it did." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "On a single attempt, Claude Opus 5.5 is first at 67.16%, Claude Opus 5 at 66.50%, GPT-5.4 at 65.36%, and GPT-6 Astra at 58.31%. The best open-weight model is Kimi K3 at 57.37%." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Now make it do that 20 times in a row." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Then it comes apart. Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Opus 5 each pass all 20 attempts on 241 of the 507 tasks. GPT-6 Astra manages 231, GPT-5.4 manages 128, and Kimi K3 just 68." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "And the failures are quiet ones. Across 121,680 valid trials, 79,853 attempts failed the executable checks, and 67.24% of those failures still terminated cleanly, invoked a state-changing tool, and reported no final tool error." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Two caveats. This is a Microsoft-run evaluation of its rivals' models, published by Microsoft, so the leaderboard is a company claim. And the paper underneath it is a preprint, so it has not been peer reviewed." }
      ]
