      "section": "Security, misuse & threat intelligence",
      "headline": "Google suspends product-vulnerability submissions to its open-source bug bounty over an influx of invalid AI reports",
      "lines": [
        { "host": "B", "text": "Google, meanwhile, has stopped taking a whole class of bug report." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "Tom's Hardware reports that Google suspended product vulnerability submissions to its Open Source Software Vulnerability Reward Program over an influx of invalid AI-driven reports. It was announced in a Google post on X on October 1st, effective the same day, with an update on the programme promised by the first quarter of 2027." },
        { "host": "B", "text": "Supply-chain reports are unaffected, and so are product reports filed before October 1st. Google said it may still take some product bugs through its Cloud programme." },
        { "host": "A", "text": "That's a single source, and only one outlet carried it. The line about maintainers being overwhelmed by reports that turned out to be unexploitable hallucinations is Tom's Hardware reporting it, not a Google count, and no figure for how many invalid reports arrived has been published." }
